  "output": "I'll analyze the provided codebase snippets now.\n\n## Performance Analysis: VoidRift\n\n---\n\n### 1. N+1 Patterns\n\n**`src/bootstrap/validate.ts:35` — File read per skill in a loop**\n\n```typescript\n// Current: O(n) synchronous file reads, one per skill\nfor (const skill of skills.indexed) {\n  const raw = require(\"fs\").readFileSync(skill.filePath, \"utf-8\"); // disk hit every iteration\n  // ...\n}\n```\n\n```typescript\n// Fix: read all skill files once, upfront, or cache in SkillManager\n// Better: batch with Promise.all if async reads are available, or\n// store raw frontmatter in SkillEntry at index time so this loop\n// reads from memory instead of disk.\nfor (const skill of skills.indexed) {\n  const raw = skill.rawFrontmatter ?? readFileSync(skill.filePath, \"utf-8\");\n}\n```\n\n**`src/bootstrap/validate.ts:51` — O(n) array lookup inside a loop**\n\n```typescript\n// Current: Array.includes is O(agents) per id → O(skills × agents) total\nconst allAgentIds = [...agents.listInteractive().map(a => a.id), ...agents.listTask().map(a => a.id)];\nconst invalidAgents = skill.agents.filter(id => !allAgentIds.includes(id));\n\n// Fix: Set for O(1) lookups\nconst agentIdSet = new Set([\n  ...agents.listInteractive().map(a => a.id),\n  ...agents.listTask().map(a => a.id),\n]);\nconst invalidAgents = skill.agents.filter(id => !agentIdSet.has(id));\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. No React in this Codebase\n\nThe provided context is a Node.js CLI/backend framework. There are no React components. If there's a TUI layer using Ink (React for terminals), that code wasn't included — the React re-renders category doesn't apply to what's shown here.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Caching Opportunities\n\n**`src/adapters/factory.ts:50` — New model client on every call**\n\n`createTierAdapter(\"flash\", config)` is called in two hot paths: `summarizer.ts` (called per file during indexing) and the MCP sampling handler in `cli.ts`. Each call constructs a new `ChatOpenAI`/`ChatAnthropic` object, losing any internal connection pool or retry state.\n\n```typescript\n// Fix: memoize by modelName + config hash\nconst _clientCache = new Map<string, BaseChatModel>();\n\nfunction createClient(config: ModelConfig, maxConcurrency?: number): BaseChatModel {\n  const key = `${config.protocol}:${config.model}:${config.baseUrl}:${maxConcurrency}`;\n  if (_clientCache.has(key)) return _clientCache.get(key)!;\n  const client = _buildClient(config, maxConcurrency); // existing switch block\n  _clientCache.set(key, client);\n  return client;\n}\n```\n\n**`src/codemap/cache.ts:47` — Synchronous disk write on every cache entry**\n\n`IndexCache.set()` calls `this.save()` immediately, which does a full `JSON.stringify` + blocking `writeFileSync` for every indexed file. During a full workspace scan this fires hundreds of times.\n\n```typescript\n// Current\npublic set(filePath: string, sha256: string, summary: string, totalLines: number): void {\n  this.data[filePath] = { sha256, summary, totalLines, lastIndexed: Date.now() };\n  this.save(); // blocking write every time\n}\n\n// Fix: debounce the write\nprivate _saveTimer: ReturnType<typeof setTimeout> | null = null;\n\npublic set(filePath: string, sha256: string, summary: string, totalLines: number): void {\n  this.data[filePath] = { sha256, summary, totalLines, lastIndexed: Date.now() };\n  if (this._saveTimer) clearTimeout(this._saveTimer);\n  this._saveTimer = setTimeout(() => { this._saveTimer = null; this.save(); }, 500);\n}\n\npublic flush(): void {\n  if (this._saveTimer) { clearTimeout(this._saveTimer); this._saveTimer = null; }\n  this.save();\n}\n```\n\nCall `flush()` at the end of a full indexing pass.\n\n**`src/codemap/index.ts` — `generateCodeMap` not cached between calls**\n\n`generateCodeMap` re-walks the entire workspace on every invocation with no result cache. It's called from `cli.ts` at startup, but also re-invocable afterward.\n\n```typescript\nlet _codeMapCache: string | null = null;\nlet _codeMapStale = true;\n\n// Invalidate on FILE_* bus events in bootstrap\nexport function invalidateCodeMap(): void { _codeMapStale = true; }\n\nexport function generateCodeMap(workspaceRoot: string): string {\n  if (!_codeMapStale && _codeMapCache !== null) return _codeMapCache;\n  const entries = walk(workspaceRoot, workspaceRoot, 0);\n  _codeMapCache = formatTree(entries);\n  _codeMapStale = false;\n  return _codeMapCache;\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 4. Memory Leaks\n\n**`src/logging/audit.ts:45` — Listener accumulation if `attach()` called multiple times**\n\n`attach()` subscribes to 15+ bus events and returns a cleanup function. If the caller loses the return value or `attach()` is called again (e.g., after a reconnect), all prior listeners remain registered silently. The `setMaxListeners(100)` in `EventBus` masks this.\n\n```typescript\n// Fix: guard against double-attach\nexport class AuditLogger {\n  private _detach: (() => void) | null = null;\n\n  attach(bus: EventBus): () => void {\n    if (this._detach) {\n      this._detach(); // clean up previous listeners before re-attaching\n    }\n    const unsubs: Array<() => void> = [];\n    // ... subscriptions ...\n    const cleanup = () => { unsubs.forEach(u => u()); this._detach = null; };\n    this._detach = cleanup;\n    return cleanup;\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**`src/bootstrap/cli.ts` — 120s timeout per elicitation holds closure references**\n\nEvery call to `mcp.setElicitationHandler` callback creates a new Promise, `setTimeout`, and `bus.subscribe`. If many elicitations are pending, each holds `unsub` + `resolve` for up to 2 minutes. This isn't a leak per se, but under rapid-fire MCP calls it'll queue up substantial closure memory.\n\n```typescript\n// Fix: track pending elicitations and cancel stale ones\nconst pendingElicitations = new Map<string, { unsub: () => void; timer: ReturnType<typeof setTimeout> }>();\n\nmcp.setElicitationHandler(async (message: string) => {\n  return new Promise((resolve) => {\n    const requestId = `elicit-${Date.now()}`;\n    const cleanup = (result: { action: string }) => {\n      const pending = pendingElicitations.get(requestId);\n      if (pending) { clearTimeout(pending.timer); pending.unsub(); pendingElicitations.delete(requestId); }\n      resolve(result);\n    };\n    container.bus.publish(\"TOOL_CONFIRMATION_REQUEST\", { ... });\n    const unsub = container.bus.subscribe(\"TOOL_CONFIRMATION_RESPONSE\", (event: any) => {\n      if (event.payload.requestId === requestId)\n        cleanup(event.payload.approved ? { action: \"accept\" } : { action: \"deny\" });\n    });\n    const timer = setTimeout(() => cleanup({ action: \"deny\" }), 120_000);\n    pendingElicitations.set(requestId, { unsub, timer });\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### 5. Redundant Computations\n\n**`src/bootstrap/validate.ts:34` — `require(\"fs\")` inside a hot loop**\n\n```typescript\n// Current: requires module resolution machinery on each iteration\nconst raw = require(\"fs\").readFileSync(skill.filePath, \"utf-8\");\n\n// Fix: use the top-level import (readFileSync is already available)\nimport { readFileSync } from \"fs\";\n// ...\nconst raw = readFileSync(skill.filePath, \"utf-8\");\n```\n\n**`src/codemap/index.ts:extractSymbols` — Split + regex on every line of every file**\n\n`extractSymbols` calls `content.split(\"\\n\")` and then runs 3 regexes against every line. For large files this is fine, but the regexes are re-compiled on each call. Hoist them to module-level constants:\n\n```typescript\n// Current: compiled fresh on every extractSymbols() invocation\nconst exportMatch = trimmed.match(\n  /^export\\s+(?:default\\s+)?(?:async\\s+)?(function|class|interface|type|const|let|enum)\\s+(\\w+)/\n);\n\n// Fix: compile once at module level\nconst EXPORT_RE = /^export\\s+(?:default\\s+)?(?:async\\s+)?(function|class|interface|type|const|let|enum)\\s+(\\w+)/;\nconst DEFAULT_EXPORT_RE = /^export\\s+default\\s+\\w/;\nconst TOP_LEVEL_RE = /^(?:async\\s+)?(function|class|interface|type|enum)\\s+(\\w+)/;\n```\n\n---\n\n### Priority Summary\n\n| Issue | Impact | Effort |\n|---|---|---|\n| `IndexCache.save()` on every write | High — blocks event loop during indexing | Low |\n| Model client memoization | Medium — unnecessary object churn on every summarize | Low |\n| Agent ID Set vs Array.includes | Medium — O(skills × agents) at startup validation | Low |\n| AuditLogger double-attach guard | Medium — silent listener accumulation | Low |\n| `generateCodeMap` result caching | Medium — full walk on every call | Medium |\n| Regex hoisting in `extractSymbols` | Low — micro-optimization | Trivial |\n",
